A||||5||deceler8||Hey 84Bill...another computer question...||||1||
Z||000000||deceler8||07-24-2001||05:22 PM||||I have this Pentium laptop with Windows 95 and a Motorola Montana modem (33.6).<P>I can't seem to get the system to properly recognize this modem. When I go through Windows install, it will only recognize it as a standard PCMCIA modem and it will only connect at about 24,000 bytes.<P>I know the thing is a dinosaur, and I only use it occasionally, but it would be nice if the thing actually connected faster.<P>Can you think of anything I'm doing wrong, or is there a better way to install the modem ?<P>I do have the driver disk, but Windows never asks for it. Is it possible the modem is toast ? Should I just trash it and get a 56K which will probably connect at no better than 38K (hey, I live in the boonies)...<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/deceler8_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||DecadenceR||07-24-2001||05:57 PM||||I had this problem for a while with my old laptop. de-install any modems that are listed in teh control panel. All of em. Every one.<BR>Then, go to install hardware. Don't let it detect the hardware itself. Instead, click the "Have Disk" button. Install it that way. Hopefully you'll be okay. <BR>But remember, if the modem is old, or it's been dropped, it's not unlikely for it to go bad. But if you're getting a connection, it should be okay. Check your ISP settings too. But if you have the spare cash, I'd get a new one while I was at it. They're pretty inexpensive.<p>[This message has been edited by DecadenceR (edited 07-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||jake1852||07-24-2001||06:01 PM||||dont let windows handle ANYTHING for you, EVER! like the last guy said, use your disk, and you will get the proper results. if you install the disk, and it still will only connect slowly, then it is not your computer, but rather your isp||||reg||1
Z||000003||AusFiero||07-24-2001||06:28 PM||||Try going to the motorlla site and see if you can download a copy of the original modem driver install disk. Install it with it. <BR>I had a modem once that would wok slower as a standard, used the factory install disc and it went back to speed.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000004||84Bill||07-26-2001||09:25 AM||||Hey Dec do what Aus said, try to get the drivers for that spacific card.||||reg||1
